{
  "work_id": "titus-shatberdi/gregory-of-nyssa-de-hominis-opificio",
  "source_path": "titus-shatberdi/gregory-of-nyssa-de-hominis-opificio.json",
  "source_language": "oge",
  "target_language": "eng",
  "provenance": {
    "claude-opus-5-5/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-11-04": {
      "model": "claude-opus-5-5",
      "prompt_version": "bulk-2026-10-12",
      "date": "2026-11-04",
      "script": "__main__"
    }
  },
  "translations": [
    {
      "chunk_id": "titus-shatberdi/gregory-of-nyssa-de-hominis-opificio#Satb.HomOp.18.s1",
      "source_sha256": "0bd5a29d15a8e21f",
      "provenance": "claude-opus-5-5/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-11-04",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "Chapter 18. He spoke about the eighteenth chapter as follows: the brutish impulse rooted in us comes from our kinship with the beasts. In the same way, in this life of growth and increase, it was stamped on the nature of those"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "titus-shatberdi/gregory-of-nyssa-de-hominis-opificio#Satb.HomOp.18.s2",
      "source_sha256": "a0712ce651b35d2c",
      "provenance": "claude-opus-5-5/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-11-04",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "who were changed. In place of the glory of the angels, this brutish growth and increase was planted among them."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "titus-shatberdi/gregory-of-nyssa-de-hominis-opificio#Satb.HomOp.18.s3",
      "source_sha256": "5522e5e4ad99e74e",
      "provenance": "claude-opus-5-5/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-11-04",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "I think this is why David the prophet recalled the wretched state of human nature and said: \"Man was in honour and did not understand.\""
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "titus-shatberdi/gregory-of-nyssa-de-hominis-opificio#Satb.HomOp.18.s4",
      "source_sha256": "1dadb4ad907e80ce",
      "provenance": "claude-opus-5-5/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-11-04",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "By \"honour\" he meant likeness to the angels. That is why he said man's condition was lower than that of the beasts, which have no reason."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "titus-shatberdi/gregory-of-nyssa-de-hominis-opificio#Satb.HomOp.18.s5",
      "source_sha256": "fcd63e7cbaec9506",
      "provenance": "claude-opus-5-5/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-11-04",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "He truly became like them, for anyone who has changed that life by turning toward material things is brutish."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "titus-shatberdi/gregory-of-nyssa-de-hominis-opificio#Satb.HomOp.18.s6",
      "source_sha256": "0b6411416e8ae0e3",
      "provenance": "claude-opus-5-5/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-11-04",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "Because of this, I think, the many passions come into human life, since we are not at all far removed from the beasts."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "titus-shatberdi/gregory-of-nyssa-de-hominis-opificio#Satb.HomOp.18.s7",
      "source_sha256": "6845a5bb1f42db4d",
      "provenance": "claude-opus-5-5/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-11-04",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "The evidence is this: the affliction found among the beasts is also found among us."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "titus-shatberdi/gregory-of-nyssa-de-hominis-opificio#Satb.HomOp.18.s8",
      "source_sha256": "d82659cf2f2dd174",
      "provenance": "claude-opus-5-5/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-11-04",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "It is not right to say that this affliction in us came from our likeness to the Godhead."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "titus-shatberdi/gregory-of-nyssa-de-hominis-opificio#Satb.HomOp.18.s9",
      "source_sha256": "6ab8605a562a7975",
      "provenance": "claude-opus-5-5/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-11-04",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "Rather, the brutish life had been made beforehand in the creation we spoke of first, as the pattern of its causes."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "titus-shatberdi/gregory-of-nyssa-de-hominis-opificio#Satb.HomOp.18.s10",
      "source_sha256": "75a431ad8eddb481",
      "provenance": "claude-opus-5-5/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-11-04",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "Since man acquired reproduction like that of the beasts, the other things that belong to their nature were also joined to him."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "titus-shatberdi/gregory-of-nyssa-de-hominis-opificio#Satb.HomOp.18.s11",
      "source_sha256": "a2d2922c7989702f",
      "provenance": "claude-opus-5-5/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-11-04",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "For the anger found among people cannot be a likeness of the image of the Godhead,"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "titus-shatberdi/gregory-of-nyssa-de-hominis-opificio#Satb.HomOp.18.s12",
      "source_sha256": "8e5b3b5e2285203e",
      "provenance": "claude-opus-5-5/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-11-04",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "and it is not right to attribute to that glorious nature any love of pleasure, or any cowardice born of fear,"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "titus-shatberdi/gregory-of-nyssa-de-hominis-opificio#Satb.HomOp.18.s13",
      "source_sha256": "90e7ea324adb406b",
      "provenance": "claude-opus-5-5/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-11-04",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "or any rashness, or love of greed, or hatred of what is slighted."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "titus-shatberdi/gregory-of-nyssa-de-hominis-opificio#Satb.HomOp.18.s14",
      "source_sha256": "0176a5dc4b72aeb2",
      "provenance": "claude-opus-5-5/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-11-04",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "All these things, and things like them, are far from the likeness of the Godhead. Man drew all of them from his brutish part."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "titus-shatberdi/gregory-of-nyssa-de-hominis-opificio#Satb.HomOp.18.s15",
      "source_sha256": "1d1e0eb1a1cbb7ad",
      "provenance": "claude-opus-5-5/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-11-04",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "For everything that brutish life acquired to preserve its kind, and everything that was wholly mixed into that life,"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "titus-shatberdi/gregory-of-nyssa-de-hominis-opificio#Satb.HomOp.18.s16",
      "source_sha256": "c664aa66a355591c",
      "provenance": "claude-opus-5-5/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-11-04",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "passed over to man and remained in him. So carnivorous animals are to be feared because of their fierce anger,"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "titus-shatberdi/gregory-of-nyssa-de-hominis-opificio#Satb.HomOp.18.s17",
      "source_sha256": "fd66fb2fdbc55184",
      "provenance": "claude-opus-5-5/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-11-04",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "and animals that bear many young are given to desire. Cowardice and fearfulness keep the timid safe,"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "titus-shatberdi/gregory-of-nyssa-de-hominis-opificio#Satb.HomOp.18.s18",
      "source_sha256": "d1ee97eae74952fc",
      "provenance": "claude-opus-5-5/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-11-04",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "and fearfulness lets them escape from the stronger. The gluttonous eaters are distressed in times of want."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "titus-shatberdi/gregory-of-nyssa-de-hominis-opificio#Satb.HomOp.18.s19",
      "source_sha256": "5404d1453bb14c70",
      "provenance": "claude-opus-5-5/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-11-04",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "All these things, and things like them, were joined to human nature through our kinship with the beasts."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "titus-shatberdi/gregory-of-nyssa-de-hominis-opificio#Satb.HomOp.18.s20",
      "source_sha256": "499f220ee0f6055c",
      "provenance": "claude-opus-5-5/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-11-04",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "Skilled painters sometimes paint a picture meant to amaze people,"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "titus-shatberdi/gregory-of-nyssa-de-hominis-opificio#Satb.HomOp.18.s21",
      "source_sha256": "4d29e984a251d21a",
      "provenance": "claude-opus-5-5/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-11-04",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "showing two images in a single head. In the same way, I think, the likeness in man is twofold."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "titus-shatberdi/gregory-of-nyssa-de-hominis-opificio#Satb.HomOp.18.s22",
      "source_sha256": "1a245cb9fcf06dc9",
      "provenance": "claude-opus-5-5/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-11-04",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "The subtlety of the mind is divine, because it is made like the beauty of the Godhead."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "titus-shatberdi/gregory-of-nyssa-de-hominis-opificio#Satb.HomOp.18.s23",
      "source_sha256": "86c456f454aa8f23",
      "provenance": "claude-opus-5-5/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-11-04",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "But the form in which the affliction has settled is like the beasts."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "titus-shatberdi/gregory-of-nyssa-de-hominis-opificio#Satb.HomOp.18.s24",
      "source_sha256": "7bd34706540c490b",
      "provenance": "claude-opus-5-5/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-11-04",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "For at times irrationality follows, through the tendency toward fellowship with the beasts, until the evil covers over the good."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "titus-shatberdi/gregory-of-nyssa-de-hominis-opificio#Satb.HomOp.18.s25",
      "source_sha256": "fb0883cd0d84142e",
      "provenance": "claude-opus-5-5/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-11-04",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "For if anyone turns the work of the mind toward such things, and forces himself to become a slave to such passions,"
    }
  ]
}
